.TH MTAB 4
.SH NAME
mtab \- mounted file system table
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmtab\fR resides in directory \fB/etc\fR and contains a table of devices mounted by the \fBmount\fR command. \fBumount\fR removes entries.
.PP
Each entry is 64 bytes long; the first 32 are the null-padded name of the place where the special file is mounted; the second 32 are the null-padded name of the special file. The special file has all its directories stripped away; that is, everything through the last '/' is thrown away.
.PP
This table is present only so people can look at it. It does not matter to \fBmount\fR if there are duplicated entries nor to \fBumount\fR if a name cannot be found.
.SH FILES
/etc/mtab
.SH "SEE ALSO"
mount(1)
.sp
